    "course_pol_en": "\tYou are allowed two absences (equivalent to 4 hours). If you miss more than 4 hours, with or without valid reasons, two points will be deducted from your semester grade for each additional hour of absence.\n\tArriving 15 minutes late or more will be counted as a one-hour absence.\n\tStudents who miss class are responsible for all materials presented and discussed in class, as well as for any assignments due. \n\tQuizzes will not be made up, as the two lowest quiz grades will be dropped. Students with perfect attendance will have their four lowest quiz grades excluded from the final grade. \n\tA deduction of 10 points will be applied for every 24-hour period an assignment is late. No assignment will be accepted after 5 days.",
    "course_rem": null,
    "course_rem_en": null,
    "ais_meno": null,
    "ais_meno_en": "<div>For all graded activities in this course, your work must be <u>essentially your own and newly produced</u>. If it is discovered that the work you submitted a) was not written by yourself (including AI-generated work), b) was used for another course, or c) contains <em>plagiarism</em>, then you will be penalized. The penalty is a grade of 0 for the assignment and, depending on the seriousness of the offence, possibly a failing grade for the course. <u>NOTE: You are responsible for understanding this policy; if you are involved in any case of academic dishonesty, you cannot claim ignorance.</u></div>\n",
    "ilearn_mk": "N"
  },
